1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Image from Find A Grave https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/99750452/carl-eric-nyberg 
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl Erik Nyberg married Erna Margrethe Sonne in 1927.  She moved from Denmark to live in Finland where Nyberg served as a District Governor.  They divorced in 1935. Erna Nyberg returned to Denmark with their daughter. Carl Nyberg
2 CONC  remarried.  He was killed in Summa, Kuolemajärvi (now Russian territory Pionerskoje) on February 5, 1940 (Finland WWII Casualties) and is buried in Hietaniemi Cemetery, Finland. (Find A Grave). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Judging from Nyberg's death date of Feb. 5, 1940, he was involved in the last stage of the "Winter War" with the Soviet Union, which Finland lost.  The Soviets attacked Finland on Nov. 30, 1939. The offense ended February 11, 1940
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_history_of_Finland_during_World_War_II "The Winter War was fought in three stages: the initial Soviet advance, a short lull and then a renewed Soviet offensive.[9] The war was fought mainly i
2 CONC n three areas. The Karelian Isthmus and the area of Lake Ladoga was the primary focus of the Soviet war effort. The last phase began in February 1940 with a major artillery barrage that began on the 2nd and lasted till the 11th, a
2 CONC ccompanied by reconnaissance raids at key objectives.[14] The Soviets, using new equipment and materials, also began using tactics of rotating troops from the reserve to the front, constantly applying pressure to the Finnish defen
2 CONC ders.[15] It seemed that the Red Army had inexhaustible amounts of ammunition and supplies, as attacks were always preceded by barrages, followed by aerial assaults and then random troop movements against the lines. Finnish milita
2 CONC ry and government leaders saw that the only thing left to do was to negotiate a peace treaty with Moscow.[16]"
2 CONT
2 CONT Hufvudstadsbladet, 20.02.1940, nro 49, s. 1
2 CONT https://digi.kansalliskirjasto.fi/sanomalehti/binding/2232196?page=1
2 CONT Kansalliskirjaston digitaaliset aineistot
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
