2 CONC  They divorced in 1935. Erna Nyberg returned to Denmark with their daughter. Carl Nyberg remarried.  He was killed in Summa, Kuolemajärvi (now Russian territory Pionerskoje) on February 5, 1940 (Finland WWII Casualties) and is bur
2 CONC ied in Hietaniemi Cemetery, Finland. (Find A Grave).   Judging from Nyberg's death date of Feb. 5, 1940, he was involved in the last stage of the "Winter War" with the Soviet Union, which Finland lost.  The Soviets attacked Finlan
2 CONC d on Nov. 30, 1939. The offense ended February 11, 1940.  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_history_of_Finland_during_World_War_II "The Winter War was fought in three stages: the initial Soviet advance, a short lull and then 
2 CONC a renewed Soviet offensive.[9] The war was fought mainly in three areas. The Karelian Isthmus and the area of Lake Ladoga was the primary focus of the Soviet war effort. The last phase began in February 1940 with a major artillery
2 CONC  barrage that began on the 2nd and lasted till the 11th, accompanied by reconnaissance raids at key objectives.[14] The Soviets, using new equipment and materials, also began using tactics of rotating troops from the reserve to th
2 CONC e front, constantly applying pressure to the Finnish defenders.[15] It seemed that the Red Army had inexhaustible amounts of ammunition and supplies, as attacks were always preceded by barrages, followed by aerial assaults and the
2 CONC n random troop movements against the lines. Finnish military and government leaders saw that the only thing left to do was to negotiate a peace treaty with Moscow.[16]"  Hufvudstadsbladet, 20.02.1940, nro 49, s. 1 https://digi.kan
