1 NOTE {geni:about_me} As a teenager I was a member of the YMCA in Buenos Aires. There, we started a Group of Leaders, I was elected to be it's first President during une (1) year, As Leaders we ministrated gym classes, supervised baseba
2 CONC ll and volleyball matches, acted as swimming teachers and as lifeguards at the swimming pool.
2 CONT
2 CONT During a three months period of school vacations I worked as an apprentice in a metal workshop learning to work on a lathe aside of a superficial knowledge of life in a workshop. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After my obligatory military service I worked as a "motor trainee" on the Swedish freight ship MS Pacific, from Argentina to Sweden and back, which took about three months. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On this occasion I had the happy possibility of meeting my Swedish grandmother, Emma Bong Lundberg, during the short time the ship spent in Sweden. There I also met some of my other relatives in Sweden:uncles, aunts and cousins. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the years I worked for Sandvik I made several working trips to Sweden, Denmark, Germany, Italy, Portugal and Canada. Privately I had occasion to visit Chile, Uruguay. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In Argentina I have been in Salta, Mendoza, Bariloche and many other places. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In Chile I have been in Puerto Montt, Santiago and Valparaiso. In Brasil I hav been on nost cities along the Atlantic Ocean between Rio Gande and Pelotas and Recife.  
