1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otto_Donner '''Otto Donner'''] was a Finnish linguist and politician. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Otto Donner was''' Finland’s first professor of Sanskrit and Comparative Indo-European linguistics at the University of Helsinki. His special area of expertise was the organisation of fieldwork. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He also studied''' the Finno-Ugric languages and participated in the founding of the Finno-Ugrian Society in 1883. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was an''' encouraging teacher for many young linguists, many of them becoming internationally recognized scholars in their own right. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was a''' member of the Diet of Finland 1877–1905, and minister of education 1905–1908. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His mother tongue''' was Swedish, but he was a fennoman by conviction. He belongs to the renowned [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donner_family Donner family]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He is buried''' in the Hietaniemi Cemetery in Helsinki.
2 CONT
