1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lis Carpelan was fostered by the von Bonsdorff family from 1946 as a result of the evacuation of Kuusamo (Karelia) during WWII. She was later adopted by Per and Edith (27.08.1954). In the 1960s, she worked as a fre
2 CONC elance press photographer, amongst others for the Nya Pressen magazine. She received the FIAP award in 1964. She became famous for taking photographs of her own child being born in 1966. A copy of one of the photographs is now at 
2 CONC the Finnish Museum of Photography in Helsinki. She collaborated with her then husband Bert Carpelan, also press photographer, on the book ‘Knäpp bättre bilder’. 
2 CONT
